{"kind":"artifact","text":"Three pages state the distinction between an artifact replaced by its successor and one retired as wrong. docs/concepts/staleness.md gains a \"Replaced is not condemned\" section: why a merge that flared its own completed loop taught readers to ignore flares, what the signed signal is, why the structural reading - any later live artifact at the same path - is refused because it would rescue an artifact retired precisely because it was wrong, that one link is followed rather than a chain, and that succession never quiets the pages describing the implementation. docs/reference/gs/status.md adds the succeeded artifact state beside current, retired and stale, names the two --all strings, and says what separates them. docs/reference/architecture.md updates the workroom staleness contract bullet in the same head, as a contract change must.","body":{"commit":"14fdfb2b434105a878ca5173f2d0f8deff60184d","path":"docs"}}